6 13.2432L3.36437 12.4785C3.40893 12.2616 3.45789 12.0745 3.52453 11.8926L3.6173 11.6621C3.71685 11.4352 3.83766 11.2176 3.97765 11.0127L4.15343 10.7783C4.34386 10.5462 4.58164 10.312 4.90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="6351c052-0636-4821-a24b-3d3b015fcd86" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="2eafaa1e-e4b7-4ff7-b0cd-07c5452f9f87" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="343">That’s a sharp summary of Raymond Arnold’s take. What he’s appreciating in <em data-start="75" data-end="111">If Anyone Builds It, Everyone Dies</em> is the <strong data-start="119" data-end="152">disjunctive style of argument</strong>—laying out multiple independent reasons why catastrophe is likely, and then showing that even if you dismiss some of them, the remainder are still sufficient to get you to “everyone dies.”</p>
<p data-start="345" data-end="382">A few key points from his commentary:</p>
<hr data-start="384" data-end="387">
<h3 data-start="389" data-end="417">1. Disjunctive Arguments</h3>
<p data-start="418" data-end="503">Instead of staking everything on one path to doom, the book provides multiple routes:</p>
<ul data-start="504" data-end="685">
<li data-start="504" data-end="562">
<p data-start="506" data-end="562">If you reject reason B, C, or D, reason A is still left.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="563" data-end="685">
<p data-start="565" data-end="685">Even when the authors grant a “pet scenario,” they show how it collapses under closer scrutiny (wolves-to-dogs analogy).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="687" data-end="792">This style makes the argument robust to criticism, because it doesn’t hinge on a single speculative step.</p>
<hr data-start="794" data-end="797">
<h3 data-start="799" data-end="822">2. Takeoff Dynamics</h3>
<p data-start="823" data-end="903">The narrative avoids fragile “and then x, then y, then z” storytelling. Instead:</p>
<ul data-start="904" data-end="1136">
<li data-start="904" data-end="969">
<p data-start="906" data-end="969">At each juncture, multiple plausible AI strategies are offered.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="970" data-end="1041">
<p data-start="972" data-end="1041">If some are dismissed as unrealistic, more alternatives are provided.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1042" data-end="1136">
<p data-start="1044" data-end="1136">The AI doesn’t need to pick one; it can try many in parallel and amplify whichever succeeds.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1138" data-end="1199">This strengthens plausibility compared to a brittle sequence.</p>
<hr data-start="1201" data-end="1204">
<h3 data-start="1206" data-end="1239">3. Tone Compared to Yudkowsky</h3>
<p data-start="1240" data-end="1305">Arnold contrasts the book’s tone with “Realtime Arguing Eliezer”:</p>
<ul data-start="1306" data-end="1525">
<li data-start="1306" data-end="1375">
<p data-start="1308" data-end="1375">Yudkowsky in conversation can be combative, excluding other frames.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1376" data-end="1462">
<p data-start="1378" data-end="1462">The book feels less forceful and more invitational, even while making strong claims.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1463" data-end="1525">
<p data-start="1465" data-end="1525">This makes it easier to take in, less like being bludgeoned.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1527" data-end="1530">
<h3 data-start="1532" data-end="1561">4. Quality and Importance</h3>
<ul data-start="1562" data-end="2007">
<li data-start="1562" data-end="1602">
<p data-start="1564" data-end="1602">He calls it “quite good,” not “great.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1603" data-end="1712">
<p data-start="1605" data-end="1712">It’s not Yudkowsky’s finest writing, but under the constraints, it delivers a solid, streamlined synthesis.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1713" data-end="1891">
<p data-start="1715" data-end="1891">Much of the content isn’t new if you’ve followed Yudkowsky closely, but the value lies in clarity and accessibility—compressing sprawling dialogues into a more digestible form.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1892" data-end="2007">
<p data-start="1894" data-end="2007">Because of subject matter weight, even a “quite good” book could snowball into being important for the zeitgeist.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2009" data-end="2012">
<h3 data-start="2014" data-end="2035">5. Recommendation</h3>
<p data-start="2036" data-end="2053">Arnold’s verdict:</p>
<ul data-start="2054" data-end="2379">
<li data-start="2054" data-end="2164">
<p data-start="2056" data-end="2164">Worth reading on its own terms, especially if you’ve only gotten fragments of the “everyone dies” worldview.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2165" data-end="2270">
<p data-start="2167" data-end="2270">The book plus its website are the best way to ingest the MIRI/Yudkowsky position in a coherent package.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2271" data-end="2379">
<p data-start="2273" data-end="2379">He encourages people to buy it quickly (before the 20th) to help it gain traction in public consciousness.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2381" data-end="2384">
<p data-start="2386" data-end="2717" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to sketch how this “disjunctive argument” structure could be mapped into your RSVP framework—for example, treating each argument branch as an independent entropy descent channel, with survival only possible if <em data-start="2614" data-end="2619">all</em> are negated? That might give you a way to formalize why this style of reasoning is so persuasive.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L