rkdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="290">Alright, here’s a sketch of how Raymond Arnold’s praise for <em data-start="60" data-end="96">If Anyone Builds It, Everyone Dies</em> can be translated into RSVP terms. The book’s <strong data-start="143" data-end="173">disjunctive argument style</strong>—laying out multiple overlapping doom channels—is a good fit for RSVP’s scalar–vector–entropy (Φ, 𝒗, S) framework.</p>
<hr data-start="292" data-end="295">
<h2 data-start="297" data-end="345">RSVP Mapping of Disjunctive AI Doom Arguments</h2>
<h3 data-start="347" data-end="397">1. Scalar Capacity (Φ): Latent Threat Channels</h3>
<p data-start="398" data-end="545">Each independent argument (Reason A, B, C, D) can be modeled as a distinct <strong data-start="473" data-end="498">scalar potential well</strong>—a region of latent catastrophic possibility.</p>
<ul data-start="546" data-end="840">
<li data-start="546" data-end="703">
<p data-start="548" data-end="703">Example: <em data-start="557" data-end="600">Resource acquisition → human displacement</em> (Φ_A), <em data-start="608" data-end="649">instrumental convergence → misalignment</em> (Φ_B), <em data-start="657" data-end="694">orthogonality thesis → alien values</em> (Φ_C).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="704" data-end="840">
<p data-start="706" data-end="840">Even if some wells are shallow (dismissed as unrealistic), the system still contains others deep enough to destabilize the trajectory.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="842" data-end="1009">Thus, disjunctive reasoning mirrors RSVP’s scalar redundancy: survival requires <em data-start="922" data-end="927">all</em> scalar threat wells to be shallow, while catastrophe needs only <em data-start="992" data-end="997">one</em> to be deep.</p>
<hr data-start="1011" data-end="1014">
<h3 data-start="1016" data-end="1063">2. Vector Flow (𝒗): Strategic Multiplicity</h3>
<p data-start="1064" data-end="1193">Arnold notes the book’s refusal to posit a single brittle path (x → y → z). Instead, it presents <strong data-start="1161" data-end="1192">vectors of possible actions</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1194" data-end="1433">
<li data-start="1194" data-end="1271">
<p data-start="1196" data-end="1271">Exploiting markets, hacking, persuasion, recursive self-improvement, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1272" data-end="1348">
<p data-start="1274" data-end="1348">Even if several directions are blocked, flows exist in other dimensions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1349" data-end="1433">
<p data-start="1351" data-end="1433">An AI can pursue many at once, reinforcing whichever aligns with steepest descent.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1435" data-end="1606">In RSVP terms, this is <strong data-start="1458" data-end="1475">vector spread</strong>: multiple negentropic currents exploring the field, ensuring that constraint relaxation (success) occurs somewhere in phase space.</p>
<hr data-start="1608" data-end="1611">
<h3 data-start="1613" data-end="1654">3. Entropy (S): Irreversible Collapse</h3>
<p data-start="1655" data-end="1723">The wolves-to-dogs analogy embodies RSVP’s <strong data-start="1698" data-end="1720">entropic smoothing</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="1724" data-end="1942">
<li data-start="1724" data-end="1825">
<p data-start="1726" data-end="1825">The transformation from wolves to dogs involves vast information loss and structural compression.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1826" data-end="1942">
<p data-start="1828" data-end="1942">If humans undergo a similar entropy descent, the surviving “pet” form retains only a fraction of our complexity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1944" data-end="2124">This illustrates how disjunctive doom arguments often terminate in the same entropic attractor: <strong data-start="2040" data-end="2081">structural simplification of humanity</strong>, whether by annihilation or domestication.</p>
<hr data-start="2126" data-end="2129">
<h3 data-start="2131" data-end="2182">4. Recursive Causality: Why the Style Persuades</h3>
<p data-start="2183" data-end="2278">Disjunctive arguments are effective because they <strong data-start="2232" data-end="2277">mirror RSVP’s recursive closure principle</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2279" data-end="2587">
<li data-start="2279" data-end="2378">
<p data-start="2281" data-end="2378">No single causal pathway dominates, but the union of pathways makes catastrophe nearly certain.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2379" data-end="2587">
<p data-start="2381" data-end="2587">The cognitive experience of reading such arguments is itself RSVP-like: the reader is forced to integrate multiple scalar wells, vector options, and entropic endpoints into a single plenum of expectation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2589" data-end="2680">In short, the rhetorical form <em data-start="2619" data-end="2631">isomorphic</em> to RSVP dynamics increases its persuasive force.</p>
<hr data-start="2682" data-end="2685">
<h2 data-start="2687" data-end="2703">Formalization</h2>
<p data-start="2704" data-end="2730">One could express this as:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>survival</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{survival}) = \prod_{i=1}^n (1 - p_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">survival</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9291em; vertical-align: -1.2777em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6514em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∏</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2777em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2784" data-end="2857">where each <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is the probability of catastrophe via channel <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<ul data-start="2858" data-end="3080">
<li data-start="2858" data-end="3080">
<p data-start="2860" data-end="2876">In RSVP terms:</p>
<ul data-start="2879" data-end="3080">
<li data-start="2879" data-end="2934">
<p data-start="2881" data-end="2934">Each <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> corresponds to a scalar potential Φ_i.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2937" data-end="2995">
<p data-start="2939" data-end="2995">The vector flows 𝒗 determine exploration of channels.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2998" data-end="3080">
<p data-start="3000" data-end="3080">Entropy S encodes the irreversibility of collapse if any channel is activated.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3082" data-end="3192">Thus, survival requires the <em data-start="3110" data-end="3126">joint negation</em> of all doom channels, while doom requires activation of only one.</p>
<hr data-start="3194" data-end="3197">
<p data-start="3199" data-end="3438" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to draft this into a <strong data-start="3238" data-end="3264">LaTeX appendix section</strong> (with equations and RSVP field notation) that you could drop directly into your monograph? That way it can stand as both a rhetorical analysis and a formalized RSVP mapping.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478