</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{T}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bar</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for all </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then a necessary condition is
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bar</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> M T).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Hence required barrier height grows </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{logarithmically} in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; equivalently, holding barriers fixed while </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> grows erodes </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> exponentially.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Implications.}
(i) Cataloging countermeasures without reducing channel count </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> yields at best linear improvements in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>1/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{E}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. (ii) The only durable levers are (a) cutting channels (reduce </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>), (b) raising </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{all} barriers so their sum of rates stays below a target, and (c) altering the state space so that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{doom}})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> shrinks relative to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{safe}})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (reduce </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>). These are </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{measure-level} changes, not merely tactical patches.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
