</li>
<li data-start="863" data-end="912">
<p data-start="866" data-end="912">At <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=9</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">9</span></span></span></span>, slope is <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f'(9)=\tfrac{1}{6}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0019em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7519em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1901em; vertical-align: -0.345em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8451em;"><span style="top: -2.655em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">6</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.394em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.345em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="913" data-end="1014">
<p data-start="916" data-end="941">Approximate <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(9.1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9.1</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0167</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.0167.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(9.1)\approx f(9)+f'(9)\cdot 0.1=3+0.0167\approx 3.0167.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9.1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0519em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.0167</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3.0167.</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="1015" data-end="1064">
<p data-start="1018" data-end="1064">Compare to calculator: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0166...</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(9.1)=3.0166...</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">9.1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3.0166...</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1065" data-end="1107">
<p data-start="1068" data-end="1107">Error is tiny — the slope got us there.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1109" data-end="1244"><strong data-start="1109" data-end="1133">Extension (optional)</strong><br data-start="1133" data-end="1136">
Try with <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\sin(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">sin</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> at <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>: slope is 1, so <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin(0.1)\approx 0.1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">sin</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0.1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.1</span></span></span></span>. Compare actual value: 0.0998.</p>
<p data-start="1246" data-end="1267"><strong data-start="1246" data-end="1265">Wrap-up (5 min)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1268" data-end="1450">
<li data-start="1268" data-end="1324">
<p data-start="1270" data-end="1324">Calculus is just “use slope to guess nearby values.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1325" data-end="1370">
<p data-start="1327" data-end="1370">Error is small if you don’t step too far.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1371" data-end="1450">
<p data-start="1373" data-end="1450">You already do this when you forecast trends (weather, driving, budgeting).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1452" data-end="1455">
<h1 data-start="1457" data-end="1527">Lesson Template 2: Logic is Easy — Counterexamples &amp; Contrapositives</h1>
<p data-start="1529" data-end="1651"><strong data-start="1529" data-end="1542">Objective</strong><br data-start="1542" data-end="1545">
Logic is about checking if statements are always true. Two quick tools: counterexample and contrapositive.</p>
<p data-start="1653" data-end="1814"><strong data-start="1653" data-end="1672">Warm-up (5 min)</strong><br data-start="1672" data-end="1675">
Claim: “If it’s raining, then the ground is wet.”<br data-start="1724" data-end="1727">
Ask: Is this always true? What about sprinklers? (Counterexample: ground wet, no rain.)</p>
<p data-start="1816" data-end="1847"><strong data-start="1816" data-end="1845">Core activity (15–20 min)</strong></p>
<ol data-start="1848" data-end="2349">
<li data-start="1848" data-end="1891">
<p data-start="1851" data-end="1891">Introduce implication: “If P, then Q.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1892" data-end="2077">
<p data-start="1895" data-end="1943">Define contrapositive: “If not Q, then not P.”</p>
<ul data-start="1947" data-end="2077">
<li data-start="1947" data-end="2002">
<p data-start="1949" data-end="2002">Example: “If it’s raining, then the ground is wet.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2006" data-end="2077">
<p data-start="2008" data-end="2077">Contrapositive: “If the ground is not wet, then it is not raining.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2078" data-end="2349">
<p data-start="2081" data-end="2180">Practice: Give 3 claims, ask students to (a) find a counterexample, (b) state the contrapositive.</p>
<ul data-start="2184" data-end="2349">
<li data-start="2184" data-end="2237">
<p data-start="2186" data-end="2237">“If a number is even, then it is divisible by 4.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2241" data-end="2296">
<p data-start="2243" data-end="2296">“If someone is a teacher, then they like homework.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2300" data-end="2349">
<p data-start="2302" data-end="2349">“If an animal is a dog, then it is a mammal.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2351" data-end="2542"><strong data-start="2351" data-end="2378">Group challenge (5 min)</strong><br data-start="2378" data-end="2381">
Each group writes one “If–then” statement and hands it to another group. The other group must either (a) find a counterexample or (b) rewrite the contrapositive.</p>
<p data-start="2544" data-end="2565"><strong data-start="2544" data-end="2563">Wrap-up (5 min)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2566" data-end="2773">
<li data-start="2566" data-end="2604">
<p data-start="2568" data-end="2604">Counterexamples kill false claims.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2605" data-end="2687">
<p data-start="2607" data-end="2687">Contrapositives are always logically equivalent — a trick to reframe problems.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2688" data-end="2773">
<p data-start="2690" data-end="2773">This is all propositional logic really is: testing and rewriting “if–then” rules.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2775" data-end="2778">
<p data-start="2780" data-end="2891">These are designed to fit into a <strong data-start="2813" data-end="2837">30–40 min class slot</strong>. Teachers can adapt them as repeatable “mini-labs.”</p>
