lesson template</strong>, structured like the others. Together, they form a compact <em data-start="113" data-end="141">verification literacy pack</em> (calculus, logic, probability).</p>
<hr data-start="175" data-end="178">
<h1 data-start="180" data-end="264">Lesson Template 3: Probability is Easy — Expected Value &amp; Simple Bayesian Updating</h1>
<p data-start="266" data-end="412"><strong data-start="266" data-end="279">Objective</strong><br data-start="279" data-end="282">
Probability helps you guess outcomes under uncertainty. Two core ideas: <em data-start="354" data-end="370">expected value</em> and <em data-start="375" data-end="411">updating when you see new evidence</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="414" data-end="417">
<p data-start="419" data-end="535"><strong data-start="419" data-end="438">Warm-up (5 min)</strong><br data-start="438" data-end="441">
Ask: “A die has six sides. If you roll it many times, what’s the average number you expect?”</p>
<ul data-start="536" data-end="678">
<li data-start="536" data-end="566">
<p data-start="538" data-end="566">Students may guess 3 or 4.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="567" data-end="678">
<p data-start="569" data-end="678">Calculate: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+2+3+4+5+6)/6=3.5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">4</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">/6</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3.5</span></span></span></span>.<br data-start="604" data-end="607">
Point out: Expected value is the average result if repeated many times.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="680" data-end="683">
<p data-start="685" data-end="716"><strong data-start="685" data-end="714">Core activity (15–20 min)</strong></p>
<p data-start="718" data-end="744"><em data-start="718" data-end="742">Part A: Expected Value</em></p>
<ol data-start="745" data-end="1075">
<li data-start="745" data-end="813">
<p data-start="748" data-end="813">Scenario: A game pays $10 if a coin lands heads, $0 if tails.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="814" data-end="857">
<p data-start="817" data-end="857">EV = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5\cdot 10 + 0.5\cdot 0 = 5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">10</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="858" data-end="914">
<p data-start="861" data-end="914">Meaning: Over many flips, you average $5 per play.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="915" data-end="1075">
<p data-start="918" data-end="1030">Extend: A lottery ticket costs $1 and pays $20 with prob. 0.02. EV = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.98</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>0.58</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02\cdot 20 - 0.98\cdot 1 = -0.58</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.02</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">20</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.98</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord">0.58</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<ul data-start="1034" data-end="1075">
<li data-start="1034" data-end="1075">
<p data-start="1036" data-end="1075">Conclusion: On average, you lose money.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1077" data-end="1106"><em data-start="1077" data-end="1104">Part B: Bayesian Updating</em></p>
<ol data-start="1107" data-end="1692">
<li data-start="1107" data-end="1164">
<p data-start="1110" data-end="1164">Start with prior: “10% of students are left-handed.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1165" data-end="1256">
<p data-start="1168" data-end="1256">New evidence: “We meet a student on the fencing team. 40% of fencers are left-handed.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1257" data-end="1648">
<p data-start="1260" data-end="1285">Compute posterior odds:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>left-handed&nbsp;|&nbsp;fencer</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∝</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>fencer&nbsp;|&nbsp;left-handed</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>left-handed</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{left-handed | fencer}) \propto P(\text{fencer | left-handed})\cdot P(\text{left-handed}).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">left-handed&nbsp;|&nbsp;fencer</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">fencer&nbsp;|&nbsp;left-handed</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">left-handed</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<ul data-start="1404" data-end="1648">
<li data-start="1404" data-end="1476">
<p data-start="1406" data-end="1476">Suppose 10 out of 100 students are left-handed, 90 are right-handed.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1480" data-end="1558">
<p data-start="1482" data-end="1558">Among lefties, 40% fence (4 people). Among righties, 10% fence (9 people).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1562" data-end="1585">
<p data-start="1564" data-end="1585">Total fencers = 13.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1589" data-end="1648">
<p data-start="1591" data-end="1648">So <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>left-handed&nbsp;|&nbsp;fencer</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>13</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>31</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">%</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{left-handed | fencer})=4/13\approx 31\%</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">left-handed&nbsp;|&nbsp;fencer</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">4/13</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8056em; vertical-align: -0.0556em;"></span><span class="mord">31%</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1649" data-end="1692">
<p data-start="1652" data-end="1692">Takeaway: Evidence reshapes probability.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1694" data-end="1697">
<p data-start="1699" data-end="1920"><strong data-start="1699" data-end="1726">Group challenge (5 min)</strong><br data-start="1726" data-end="1729">
Give each group a short scenario (e.g., “bag with 3 red, 7 blue marbles” or “medical test with 95% accuracy and 1% prevalence”). Ask them to compute an expected value or update a probability.</p>
<hr data-start="1922" data-end="1925">
<p data-start="1927" data-end="1948"><strong data-start="1927" data-end="1946">Wrap-up (5 min)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1949" data-end="2242">
<li data-start="1949" data-end="2023">
<p data-start="1951" data-end="2023">Expected value tells you what happens <em data-start="1989" data-end="2001">on average</em> in repeated trials.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2024" data-end="2111">
<p data-start="2026" data-end="2111">Bayesian updating: start with a prior guess, then adjust when you see new evidence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2112" data-end="2242">
<p data-start="2114" data-end="2242">With just these, you can reason about bets, risks, and tests. Probability is not mysticism — it’s bookkeeping for uncertainty.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2244" data-end="2247">
<p data-start="2249" data-end="2289">Now you’ve got a <strong data-start="2266" data-end="2288">triad of templates</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2290" data-end="2427">
<li data-start="2290" data-end="2329">
<p data-start="2292" data-end="2329"><strong data-start="2292" data-end="2305">Calculus:</strong> Slopes as prediction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2330" data-end="2379">
<p data-start="2332" data-end="2379"><strong data-start="2332" data-end="2342">Logic:</strong> Counterexamples &amp; contrapositives.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2380" data-end="2427">
<p data-start="2382" data-end="2427"><strong data-start="2382" data-end="2398">Probability:</strong> Expected value &amp; updating.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2429" data-end="2535">These can stand as a “Verification Literacy Starter Kit” for <em data-start="2490" data-end="2508">Divided We Stand</em> or a practical appendix.</p>
