<p data-start="1984" data-end="2074">— bubble around a function of <code data-start="2014" data-end="2017">x</code>.<br data-start="2018" data-end="2021">
Applying <code data-start="2033" data-end="2036">f</code> to <code data-start="2040" data-end="2043">2</code> = <code data-start="2046" data-end="2056">Pop(f,2)</code> → reduces to <code data-start="2070" data-end="2073">3</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2076" data-end="2357">
<p data-start="2079" data-end="2112"><strong data-start="2079" data-end="2110">Leaking Chatroom connection</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2116" data-end="2357">
<li data-start="2116" data-end="2163">
<p data-start="2118" data-end="2163">Each <code data-start="2123" data-end="2134">Sphere(E)</code> is like a chatroom bubble.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2167" data-end="2220">
<p data-start="2169" data-end="2220"><code data-start="2169" data-end="2176">Merge</code> corresponds to many parallel discussions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2224" data-end="2295">
<p data-start="2226" data-end="2295"><code data-start="2226" data-end="2231">Pop</code> is the moment one bubble contributes to the global workspace.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2299" data-end="2357">
<p data-start="2301" data-end="2357">Summarization = collapse of <code data-start="2329" data-end="2336">Merge</code> into a reduced Atom.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="2359" data-end="2362">
<h2 data-start="2364" data-end="2383">RSVP Integration</h2>
<ul data-start="2384" data-end="2656">
<li data-start="2384" data-end="2468">
<p data-start="2386" data-end="2468"><strong data-start="2386" data-end="2410">Φ (scalar capacity):</strong> number of spheres in play = potential semantic density.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2469" data-end="2556">
<p data-start="2471" data-end="2556"><strong data-start="2471" data-end="2492">𝒗 (vector flow):</strong> “pop” operations = directed flows of meaning between bubbles.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2557" data-end="2656">
<p data-start="2559" data-end="2656"><strong data-start="2559" data-end="2575">S (entropy):</strong> redundancy of Merge/Nest structures; leaking summaries lower S by compressing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
