ark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="281">Alright — here’s a detailed, academic-style overview of <strong data-start="56" data-end="78">Spherepop Calculus</strong>, written as if it were a section in a monograph. It contextualizes the system, defines its primitives, and situates it against lambda calculus, Monica Anderson’s epistemology, and your RSVP framework.</p>
<hr data-start="283" data-end="286">
<h1 data-start="288" data-end="321">Spherepop Calculus: An Overview</h1>
<h2 data-start="323" data-end="351">1. Motivation and Origins</h2>
<p data-start="352" data-end="446">The <strong data-start="356" data-end="384">Spherepop Calculus (SPC)</strong> emerges from the intersection of two intellectual currents:</p>
<ol data-start="447" data-end="916">
<li data-start="447" data-end="737">
<p data-start="450" data-end="737">Monica Anderson’s <em data-start="468" data-end="488">Model-Free Methods</em> (MFMs), particularly her metaphors of <strong data-start="527" data-end="542">Bubble City</strong> (an “idea router” where bubbles of thought move, collide, and recombine) and the <strong data-start="624" data-end="644">Leaking Chatroom</strong> (a distributed epistemic architecture where topic summaries seep into a global workspace).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="738" data-end="916">
<p data-start="741" data-end="916">Classical foundations of formal systems (lambda calculus, compositional functions, logic gates), where the act of bracketing or parenthesizing defines the scope of evaluation.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="918" data-end="1433">The aim of SPC is to provide a <strong data-start="949" data-end="985">dynamic, interactional substrate</strong> for reasoning, where computation is modeled as the creation, nesting, merging, and popping of spheres. Unlike traditional calculi where syntax is privileged, SPC emphasizes <strong data-start="1159" data-end="1180">scope as geometry</strong>: entering a bubble defines a region of evaluation, leaving it completes a reduction. This mirrors the “circles of evaluation” used in educational treatments of Racket or Scheme, but pushes the metaphor further into a full-blown computational framework.</p>
<hr data-start="1435" data-end="1438">
<h2 data-start="1440" data-end="1452">2. Syntax</h2>
<p data-start="1453" data-end="1522">The formal language of SPC is built from a small set of constructors:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∣</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∣</mo><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∣</mo><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∣</mo><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E ::= a \mid \text{Sphere}(E) \mid \text{Merge}(E,E) \mid \text{Pop}(E,E) \mid \text{Nest}(E,E)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">::=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1627" data-end="1633">where:</p>
<ul data-start="1634" data-end="1960">
<li data-start="1634" data-end="1673">
<p data-start="1636" data-end="1673"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span></span> is an atomic symbol or value,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1674" data-end="1746">
<p data-start="1676" data-end="1746"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}(E)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> denotes a bubble enclosing an expression <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1747" data-end="1812">
<p data-start="1749" data-end="1812"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> places two expressions in parallel,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1813" data-end="1889">
<p data-start="1815" data-end="1889"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> models the application of one sphere to another,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1890" data-end="1960">
<p data-start="1892" data-end="1960"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> explicitly scopes <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> inside <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1962" data-end="2087">This syntax resembles λ-calculus in its minimalism, but with additional structure for parallel and hierarchical interactions.</p>
<hr data-start="2089" data-end="2092">
<h2 data-start="2094" data-end="2121">3. Operational Semantics</h2>
<h3 data-start="2123" data-end="2154">3.1 Transparency of Spheres</h3>
<p data-start="2155" data-end="2209">A sphere is an enclosure, not a computation by itself:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}(E) \leadsto E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2244" data-end="2297">unless and until it interacts through <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
<h3 data-start="2299" data-end="2325">3.2 Pop as Application</h3>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mo>⇝</mo><mtext>  </mtext><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}(\text{Sphere}(E_1),E_2) \;\leadsto\; E_1[E_2/x]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2391" data-end="2505">interpreting a sphere as an abstraction awaiting input. The act of popping substitutes the argument into the body.</p>
<h3 data-start="2507" data-end="2544">3.3 Merge as Parallel Composition</h3>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}(E_1,E_2) \leadsto \langle E_1,E_2 \rangle</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⟨</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">⟩</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2606" data-end="2738">indicating simultaneous presence in the workspace. Conceptually, this is closer to logical conjunction than to function application.</p>
<h3 data-start="2740" data-end="2769">3.4 Nest as Delayed Scope</h3>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}(E_1,E_2) \leadsto \text{Sphere}(E_1(E_2))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2830" data-end="2934">capturing the familiar intuition of parentheses: evaluation inside is postponed until explicitly popped.</p>
<hr data-start="2936" data-end="2939">
<h2 data-start="2941" data-end="2968">4. Illustrative Examples</h2>
<h3 data-start="2970" data-end="2994">4.1 Arithmetic Scope</h3>
<p data-start="2995" data-end="3031">The classical example of bracketing:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}(\text{Merge}(2,3))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3071" data-end="3145">represents <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2+3)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> awaiting a popping operation with the <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">+</span></span></span></span> operator.</p>
<h3 data-start="3147" data-end="3175">4.2 Function Abstraction</h3>
<p data-start="3176" data-end="3204">Define a function increment:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f = \text{Sphere}(\text{Pop}(x, x+1)).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3250" data-end="3264">Applying to 2:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mn>3.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}(f,2) \leadsto 3.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3.</span></span></span></span></span>
<h3 data-start="3300" data-end="3329">4.3 Distributed Reasoning</h3>
<p data-start="3330" data-end="3499">In a Leaking Chatroom interpretation, multiple conversations exist in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}(E_1,E_2,\dots,E_n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, but “leak” their summaries into the global sphere when popped.</p>
<hr data-start="3501" data-end="3504">
<h2 data-start="3506" data-end="3539">5. Relation to Lambda Calculus</h2>
<p data-start="3540" data-end="3601">SPC is a <strong data-start="3549" data-end="3600">λ-like calculus with enriched scoping operators</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3602" data-end="3923">
<li data-start="3602" data-end="3656">
<p data-start="3604" data-end="3656"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span></span></span></span> generalizes application <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f\;x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3657" data-end="3774">
<p data-start="3659" data-end="3774"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span></span></span></span> is analogous to abstraction <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda x.M)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mord">.</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, but emphasizes enclosures rather than variables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3775" data-end="3842">
<p data-start="3777" data-end="3842"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span></span></span></span> formalizes parentheses as first-class citizens.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3843" data-end="3923">
<p data-start="3845" data-end="3923"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span></span></span></span> provides a concurrency primitive absent in pure λ-calculus.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3925" data-end="4082">Thus, SPC can be seen as both a pedagogical bridge (from “circles of evaluation” to λ-calculus) and an epistemic substrate for distributed cognitive systems.</p>
<hr data-start="4084" data-end="4087">
<h2 data-start="4089" data-end="4111">6. RSVP Integration</h2>
<p data-start="4112" data-end="4170">In the Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) framework:</p>
<ul data-start="4171" data-end="4604">
<li data-start="4171" data-end="4273">
<p data-start="4173" data-end="4273"><strong data-start="4173" data-end="4200">Scalar field (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>)</strong> corresponds to the number and density of spheres (semantic potential).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4274" data-end="4393">
<p data-start="4276" data-end="4393"><strong data-start="4276" data-end="4309">Vector field (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>)</strong> corresponds to directional “pop” interactions (flows of meaning between spheres).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4394" data-end="4604">
<p data-start="4396" data-end="4604"><strong data-start="4396" data-end="4415">Entropy (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>)</strong> corresponds to redundancy and overlap in merged structures; popping operations reduce entropy by collapsing spheres, while merges increase entropy by proliferating possible interactions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4606" data-end="4827">SPC thereby functions as a microcosmic simulation of RSVP: bubbles stand in for cognitive, linguistic, or cosmological units of structure, interacting through pops (constraint relaxations) and merges (entropic branching).</p>
<hr data-start="4829" data-end="4832">
<h2 data-start="4834" data-end="4882">7. Pedagogical and Philosophical Significance</h2>
<p data-start="4883" data-end="4925">Spherepop calculus achieves several goals:</p>
<ol data-start="4926" data-end="5538">
<li data-start="4926" data-end="5068">
<p data-start="4929" data-end="5068"><strong data-start="4929" data-end="4959">Pedagogical accessibility:</strong> It reframes parentheses, scope, and evaluation in terms of a concrete, visual metaphor (spheres and pops).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5069" data-end="5251">
<p data-start="5072" data-end="5251"><strong data-start="5072" data-end="5097">Epistemic modularity:</strong> It provides a structural substrate that naturally aligns with distributed cognition (Anderson’s Model-Free Methods, global workspaces, bubble routing).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5252" data-end="5424">
<p data-start="5255" data-end="5424"><strong data-start="5255" data-end="5282">Computational richness:</strong> It embeds λ-calculus inside a broader system that admits parallelism, delayed evaluation, and higher-order scope as first-class operations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5425" data-end="5538">
<p data-start="5428" data-end="5538"><strong data-start="5428" data-end="5447">RSVP resonance:</strong> It models scalar capacity, vector flows, and entropy dynamics directly in its semantics.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="5540" data-end="5543">
<h2 data-start="5545" data-end="5568">8. Future Directions</h2>
<ul data-start="5569" data-end="6124">
<li data-start="5569" data-end="5677">
<p data-start="5571" data-end="5677"><strong data-start="5571" data-end="5588">Type Systems:</strong> Develop a dependent type system for SPC, where sphere classes encode type constraints.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5678" data-end="5815">
<p data-start="5680" data-end="5815"><strong data-start="5680" data-end="5701">Homotopy Lifting:</strong> Explore SPC–HoTT connections, treating sphere merges and pops as path-contractions and higher-order homotopies.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5816" data-end="5956">
<p data-start="5818" data-end="5956"><strong data-start="5818" data-end="5837">Implementation:</strong> Build an interpreter where bubbles are visualized objects, enabling “pop” and “merge” as tangible user interactions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5957" data-end="6124">
<p data-start="5959" data-end="6124"><strong data-start="5959" data-end="5975">Integration:</strong> Use SPC as a pedagogical scaffold for teaching both functional programming (λ-calculus) and logical reasoning (propositional and predicate logic).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6126" data-end="6129">
<p data-start="6131" data-end="6360" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to now <strong data-start="6156" data-end="6192">expand this into a LaTeX section</strong> (with formal definitions, inference rules, and reduction semantics in math mode), so it’s ready to slot into your essay or monograph as <em data-start="6329" data-end="6359">Appendix: Spherepop Calculus</em>?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 