ark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="280">Understood — we can present <strong data-start="28" data-end="56">Spherepop Calculus (SPC)</strong> on its own terms, as a formal and pedagogical system, without tying it explicitly to Monica Anderson. Below is a layered academic overview, structured to explain SPC at multiple levels: intuitive, formal, and theoretical.</p>
<hr data-start="282" data-end="285">
<h1 data-start="287" data-end="329">Spherepop Calculus: Multi-Level Overview</h1>
<h2 data-start="331" data-end="371">1. Intuitive Level: Spheres as Scopes</h2>
<p data-start="372" data-end="451">At its most accessible, SPC is a way of visualizing <strong data-start="424" data-end="448">scope and evaluation</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="452" data-end="721">
<li data-start="452" data-end="538">
<p data-start="454" data-end="538">Imagine each parenthesis in an expression as the left and right sides of a bubble.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="539" data-end="649">
<p data-start="541" data-end="649">Entering the bubble (left side) means starting evaluation; leaving it (right side) means the scope closes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="650" data-end="721">
<p data-start="652" data-end="721"><strong data-start="652" data-end="672">Popping a sphere</strong> means carrying out the evaluation it contains.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="723" data-end="950">This makes SPC a natural generalization of the “circles of evaluation” sometimes used in teaching functional programming. Where traditional syntax uses parentheses, SPC uses <strong data-start="897" data-end="908">spheres</strong> as the fundamental enclosures of meaning.</p>
<hr data-start="952" data-end="955">
<h2 data-start="957" data-end="998">2. Formal Level: Syntax and Operations</h2>
<h3 data-start="1000" data-end="1014">2.1 Syntax</h3>
<p data-start="1015" data-end="1083">Expressions <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span> are built recursively from atoms and constructors:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E ::= a \;\;|\;\; \text{Sphere}(E) \;\;|\;\; \text{Merge}(E,E) \;\;|\;\; \text{Pop}(E,E) \;\;|\;\; \text{Nest}(E,E).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">::=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<ul data-start="1208" data-end="1495">
<li data-start="1208" data-end="1244">
<p data-start="1210" data-end="1244"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span></span></span></span>: atomic symbol or constant</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1245" data-end="1299">
<p data-start="1247" data-end="1299"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}(E)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: an enclosed evaluation scope</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1300" data-end="1362">
<p data-start="1302" data-end="1362"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: two bubbles coexist in parallel</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1363" data-end="1435">
<p data-start="1365" data-end="1435"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: one sphere applies to another (application)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1436" data-end="1495">
<p data-start="1438" data-end="1495"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}(E_1,E_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: explicit hierarchical nesting</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1497" data-end="1526">2.2 Operational Semantics</h3>
<ul data-start="1527" data-end="2066">
<li data-start="1527" data-end="1620">
<p data-start="1529" data-end="1555"><strong data-start="1529" data-end="1553">Sphere Transparency:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}(E) \leadsto E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1598" data-end="1620">unless invoked by pop.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1622" data-end="1778">
<p data-start="1624" data-end="1648"><strong data-start="1624" data-end="1646">Pop (Application):</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}(\text{Sphere}(E_1),E_2) \leadsto E_1[E_2/x]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1718" data-end="1778">i.e. a bubble functions as an abstraction awaiting an input.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1780" data-end="1931">
<p data-start="1782" data-end="1805"><strong data-start="1782" data-end="1803">Merge (Parallel):</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}(E_1,E_2) \leadsto \langle E_1,E_2 \rangle</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⟨</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">⟩</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1875" data-end="1931">meaning both are active simultaneously in the workspace.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1933" data-end="2066">
<p data-start="1935" data-end="1954"><strong data-start="1935" data-end="1952">Nest (Scope):</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⇝</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}(E_1,E_2) \leadsto \text{Sphere}(E_1(E_2))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel amsrm">⇝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2023" data-end="2066">explicit bracketing that delays evaluation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2068" data-end="2071">
<h2 data-start="2073" data-end="2121">3. Functional Level: Comparison to λ-Calculus</h2>
<p data-start="2122" data-end="2164">SPC parallels λ-calculus but extends it:</p>
<ul data-start="2165" data-end="2428">
<li data-start="2165" data-end="2207">
<p data-start="2167" data-end="2207"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pop</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pop}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Pop</span></span></span></span></span> = function application.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2208" data-end="2274">
<p data-start="2210" data-end="2274"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Sphere</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sphere}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span></span></span></span> = function abstraction (encapsulated scope).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2275" data-end="2346">
<p data-start="2277" data-end="2346"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Nest</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Nest}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Nest</span></span></span></span></span> = explicit scope construction, akin to parentheses.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2347" data-end="2428">
<p data-start="2349" data-end="2428"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Merge}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Merge</span></span></span></span></span> = concurrency primitive, enabling multi-threaded evaluation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2430" data-end="2627">Thus SPC is a <strong data-start="2444" data-end="2501">λ-like calculus enriched with scoping and parallelism</strong>. It can encode the usual λ-calculus but also naturally expresses structures like multiple bubbles feeding a global workspace.</p>
<hr data-start="2629" data-end="2632">
<h2 data-start="2634" data-end="2686">4. Structural Level: Composition and Verification</h2>
<p data-start="2687" data-end="2761">SPC’s strength lies in its ability to model <strong data-start="2731" data-end="2758">compositional reasoning</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2762" data-end="3062">
<li data-start="2762" data-end="2823">
<p data-start="2764" data-end="2823"><strong data-start="2764" data-end="2773">Atoms</strong> correspond to primitive propositions or values.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2824" data-end="2880">
<p data-start="2826" data-end="2880"><strong data-start="2826" data-end="2837">Spheres</strong> enforce well-formed evaluation contexts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2881" data-end="2929">
<p data-start="2883" data-end="2929"><strong data-start="2883" data-end="2891">Pops</strong> realize substitution and reduction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2930" data-end="3005">
<p data-start="2932" data-end="3005"><strong data-start="2932" data-end="2942">Merges</strong> simulate parallel conversation or concurrent proof attempts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3006" data-end="3062">
<p data-start="3008" data-end="3062"><strong data-start="3008" data-end="3017">Nests</strong> create hierarchies of deferred evaluation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3064" data-end="3268">Because spheres themselves are first-class objects, SPC can <strong data-start="3124" data-end="3154">reason about scope as data</strong>. This makes it a candidate foundation for pedagogical tools, proof systems, or alternative programming paradigms.</p>
<hr data-start="3270" data-end="3273">
<h2 data-start="3275" data-end="3316">5. Theoretical Level: RSVP Integration</h2>
<p data-start="3317" data-end="3431">In a broader interpretive framework, SPC maps cleanly onto RSVP’s triplet of scalar, vector, and entropy fields:</p>
<ul data-start="3432" data-end="3706">
<li data-start="3432" data-end="3523">
<p data-start="3434" data-end="3523"><strong data-start="3434" data-end="3464">Scalar capacity (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>)</strong>: number of spheres in play — potential semantic density.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3524" data-end="3617">
<p data-start="3526" data-end="3617"><strong data-start="3526" data-end="3559">Vector flows (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>)</strong>: popping operations — directional transfers of meaning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3618" data-end="3706">
<p data-start="3620" data-end="3706"><strong data-start="3620" data-end="3639">Entropy (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>)</strong>: proliferating merges and redundant nests — structural disorder.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3708" data-end="3933">Evaluating a Spherepop system reduces entropy (by collapsing bubbles), while merging increases entropy (by spawning multiple possibilities). Thus SPC provides a toy model of RSVP dynamics at the level of symbolic computation.</p>
<hr data-start="3935" data-end="3938">
<h2 data-start="3940" data-end="3982">6. Philosophical Level: Why SPC Matters</h2>
<ul data-start="3983" data-end="4549">
<li data-start="3983" data-end="4118">
<p data-start="3985" data-end="4118"><strong data-start="3985" data-end="4014">Pedagogical Accessibility</strong>: SPC reimagines complex topics (functions, scope, evaluation) in terms of intuitive bubbles and pops.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4119" data-end="4239">
<p data-start="4121" data-end="4239"><strong data-start="4121" data-end="4145">Cognitive Modularity</strong>: Spheres as units of thought model how parallel reasoning can converge into shared results.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4240" data-end="4379">
<p data-start="4242" data-end="4379"><strong data-start="4242" data-end="4274">Computational Expressiveness</strong>: SPC can simulate λ-calculus but also adds concurrency, explicit scoping, and structural manipulation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4380" data-end="4549">
<p data-start="4382" data-end="4549"><strong data-start="4382" data-end="4405">Foundational Bridge</strong>: It offers a path from logic gates and compositional functions to higher-level constructs like the calculus of constructions and type theory.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4551" data-end="4554">
<h2 data-start="4556" data-end="4579">7. Future Directions</h2>
<ol data-start="4580" data-end="5085">
<li data-start="4580" data-end="4689">
<p data-start="4583" data-end="4689"><strong data-start="4583" data-end="4599">Type Systems</strong>: Equip SPC with dependent types, where sphere “colors” or “labels” enforce constraints.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4690" data-end="4804">
<p data-start="4693" data-end="4804"><strong data-start="4693" data-end="4721">Graphical Implementation</strong>: Build interpreters or visual programming tools where spheres are literal nodes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4805" data-end="4932">
<p data-start="4808" data-end="4932"><strong data-start="4808" data-end="4831">Homotopy Extensions</strong>: Treat sphere merges and pops as homotopies, leading toward connections with Homotopy Type Theory.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4933" data-end="5085">
<p data-start="4936" data-end="5085"><strong data-start="4936" data-end="4969">Integration with Verification</strong>: Use SPC as a foundation for teaching students how formal reasoning emerges from simple compositional operations.</p>
</li>
</ol>
