<hr data-start="12576" data-end="12579">
<h1 data-start="12581" data-end="12638">9. Practical note on <code data-start="12604" data-end="12611">Merge</code> as Σ vs. commutative merge</h1>
<p data-start="12640" data-end="12934">If you prefer <code data-start="12654" data-end="12661">Merge</code> to be a <strong data-start="12670" data-end="12692">commutative monoid</strong> (order-insensitive), take it as a Σ-fold over a multiset representation (e.g., Church-encoded finite bags) with a canonical ordering for <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_1,\pi_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. All typing and semantics above go through unchanged; proofs use the multiset invariant.</p>
<hr data-start="12936" data-end="12939">
<h1 data-start="12941" data-end="12968">10. Where to take it next</h1>
<ul data-start="12970" data-end="13498">
<li data-start="12970" data-end="13143">
<p data-start="12972" data-end="13143"><strong data-start="12972" data-end="12997">Refinements &amp; proofs:</strong> add a refinement type <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">R</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">i</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">s</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>o</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">D</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">o</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">o</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">m</mi></mrow><mo>⇒</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Risk}(w) := \{\,o:O \mid o=\mathsf{Doom}\Rightarrow \phi(w)\,\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Risk</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Doom</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> to make “proof-carrying safe reasons” explicit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="13144" data-end="13347">
<p data-start="13146" data-end="13347"><strong data-start="13146" data-end="13173">Time-dependent hazards:</strong> encode <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>×</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">T</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">i</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">m</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">e</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">R</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">e</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">a</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_i: W\times \mathsf{Time}\to \mathsf{Real}_{\ge 0}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Time</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9396em; vertical-align: -0.2452em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Real</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">≥</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2452em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, define <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_i(w,t)=1-\exp(-\int_0^t\kappa_i(w,s)\,ds)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vli