ll break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="314">Absolutely—here’s a small, runnable <strong data-start="36" data-end="64">Spherepop Calculus (SPC)</strong> prototype in Python. It implements the core term constructors (<code data-start="128" data-end="136">Sphere</code>, <code data-start="138" data-end="143">Pop</code>, <code data-start="145" data-end="152">Merge</code>, <code data-start="154" data-end="160">Nest</code>, <code data-start="162" data-end="168">Atom</code>, <code data-start="170" data-end="175">Var</code>), capture-avoiding substitution, a CBV evaluator, and (optionally) a simple probabilistic choice. It also includes ready-to-run demos for:</p>
<ul data-start="316" data-end="420">
<li data-start="316" data-end="364">
<p data-start="318" data-end="364">disjunctive doom (FoldOr over merged reasons),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="365" data-end="420">
<p data-start="367" data-end="420">probabilistic channels <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (independent hazards).</p>
</li>
</ul>
