p-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="309">Great — thanks for pasting your earlier <strong data-start="40" data-end="71">HTML/JS interactive version</strong>. That gives me a clear sense: you already had <strong data-start="118" data-end="152">bubbles with click-to-evaluate</strong>, with nice popping and shaking animations. We can merge that with the <strong data-start="223" data-end="246">Spherepop prototype</strong> so you can step SPC reductions interactively in the browser.</p>
<p data-start="311" data-end="373">Here’s a minimal <strong data-start="328" data-end="365">browser-side Spherepop visualizer</strong> that:</p>
<ul data-start="374" data-end="594">
<li data-start="374" data-end="431">
<p data-start="376" data-end="431">renders SPC terms as nested circles (like your code),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="432" data-end="498">
<p data-start="434" data-end="498">lets you click a bubble to <strong data-start="461" data-end="468">pop</strong> (perform a reduction step),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="499" data-end="545">
<p data-start="501" data-end="545">animates the bubble disappearing/reducing,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="546" data-end="594">
<p data-start="548" data-end="594">re-labels the circle with the reduced value.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="596" data-end="599">
