<hr data-start="3830" data-end="3833">
<h3 data-start="3835" data-end="3853">What this does</h3>
<ul data-start="3854" data-end="4137">
<li data-start="3854" data-end="3896">
<p data-start="3856" data-end="3896">Renders a <strong data-start="3866" data-end="3876">bubble</strong> for the SPC term.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3897" data-end="4137">
<p data-start="3899" data-end="3910">On click:</p>
<ul data-start="3913" data-end="4137">
<li data-start="3913" data-end="4055">
<p data-start="3915" data-end="4055">If it reduces (β-reduction with <code data-start="3947" data-end="3955">Sphere</code> + <code data-start="3958" data-end="3964">Atom</code> arg), you see the <strong data-start="3983" data-end="4004">popping animation</strong>, then it updates to the reduced result (<code data-start="4045" data-end="4051">Doom</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4058" data-end="4137">
<p data-start="4060" data-end="4137">If it can’t reduce, you see a <strong data-start="4090" data-end="4109">shake animation</strong> (like your earlier code).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4139" data-end="4142">
<h3 data-start="4144" data-end="4157">Next step</h3>
<p data-start="4158" data-end="4165">We can:</p>
<ol data-start="4166" data-end="4413">
<li data-start="4166" data-end="4254">
<p data-start="4169" data-end="4254">Extend this to handle <strong data-start="4191" data-end="4200">Merge</strong> visually (multiple child bubbles in one container).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4255" data-end="4350">
<p data-start="4258" data-end="4350">Show <strong data-start="4263" data-end="4290">sequences of reductions</strong> step by step (so you can watch an entire term normalize).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4351" data-end="4413">
<p data-start="4354" data-end="4413">Port this JSON → <strong data-start="4371" data-end="4383">three.js</strong> for interactive 3D spheres.</p>
</li>
