y — what I meant was: instead of the <strong data-start="43" data-end="64">“Step All” button</strong> jumping directly to the fully normalized form, it can <em data-start="119" data-end="176">play through the whole reduction sequence automatically</em>, faster than clicking by hand. Think of it as an animation that “pops” each reducible bubble one after another in quick succession (say 200–300ms per step).</p>
