n:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div class="absolute flex h-8 w-3 origin-center items-center justify-center" style="opacity: 0; transform: scale(0);"><div class="bg-token-text-primary h-3 w-3 rounded-full"></div></div><div class="relative my-1 min-h-6"><div class="relative flex origin-top-left flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-clip" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><div class="relative w-full text-start"><div class="flex w-full flex-col items-start justify-between text-start"><button class="flex w-full items-center gap-0.5"><span class=""><span class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate text-start align-middle text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary" style="opacity: 1;">Thought for 5s</span></span></button></div></div></span><div class="max-w-[calc(0.8*var(--thread-content-max-width,40rem))]"></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="182f0478-ea98-46ab-81e7-6fa4b3795aef" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="186">Awesome—here’s a <strong data-start="17" data-end="44">drop-in LaTeX extension</strong> that adds a <strong data-start="57" data-end="86">probabilistic typing rule</strong> for <code data-start="91" data-end="99">Choice</code>. I’m giving you two clean options so you can pick the style that best fits your paper:</p>
<ul data-start="188" data-end="488">
<li data-start="188" data-end="315">
<p data-start="190" data-end="315"><strong data-start="190" data-end="221">Option A (internal choice):</strong> <code data-start="222" data-end="237">Choice(p,t,u)</code> has the <strong data-start="246" data-end="259">same type</strong> as its branches; probability is a value of type <code data-start="308" data-end="314">Prob</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="316" data-end="488">
<p data-start="318" data-end="488"><strong data-start="318" data-end="341">Option B (monadic):</strong> <code data-start="342" data-end="350">Choice</code> returns a <strong data-start="361" data-end="377">distribution</strong> <code data-start="378" data-end="396">\mathsf{Dist}(A)</code>, with <code data-start="403" data-end="411">return</code>/<code data-start="412" data-end="418">bind</code> rules (useful if you want semantic compositionality for probability).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="490" data-end="554">You can paste either block <strong data-start="517" data-end="526">after</strong> the rules you already have.</p>
<hr data-start="556" data-end="559">
