o your uploaded <strong data-start="31" data-end="57">Spherepop Calculus.pdf</strong>, and here’s how it already frames SPC in a <strong data-start="101" data-end="129">formal categorical style</strong>, which we can align with the BNF/type-theory presentation we built earlier:</p>
<hr data-start="207" data-end="210">
<h2 data-start="212" data-end="233">What’s in your PDF</h2>
<ol data-start="235" data-end="1351">
<li data-start="235" data-end="567">
<p data-start="238" data-end="264"><strong data-start="238" data-end="262">Monoidal Pop Functor</strong></p>
<ul data-start="268" data-end="567">
<li data-start="268" data-end="311">
<p data-start="270" data-end="311">Defines <code data-start="278" data-end="308">Pop : Sphere → [Field,Field]</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="315" data-end="413">
<p data-start="317" data-end="413">Specifies how Pop acts on objects (regions, fields), morphisms, tensor products, and the unit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="417" data-end="485">
<p data-start="419" data-end="485">Provides associator, left/right unitors, and coherence theorems.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="489" data-end="567">
