<hr data-start="1353" data-end="1356">
<h2 data-start="1358" data-end="1404">How to Integrate with the BNF/Typing System</h2>
<ul data-start="1406" data-end="2102">
<li data-start="1406" data-end="1562">
<p data-start="1408" data-end="1562"><strong data-start="1408" data-end="1444">BNF + Typing Rules (λ/CoC style)</strong><br data-start="1444" data-end="1447">
Give the syntactic surface (Sphere, Pop, Merge, Choice, etc.), typing, and β-reduction rules (what we drafted).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1564" data-end="1934">
<p data-start="1566" data-end="1668"><strong data-start="1566" data-end="1610">Category-Theoretic Layer (from your PDF)</strong><br data-start="1610" data-end="1613">
Show how these constructs are modeled semantically:</p>
<ul data-start="1671" data-end="1934">
<li data-start="1671" data-end="1717">
<p data-start="1673" data-end="1717"><code data-start="1673" data-end="1681">Sphere</code> ↔ objects/1-cells in <strong data-start="1703" data-end="1714">Sphere²</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1720" data-end="1798">
<p data-start="1722" data-end="1798"><code data-start="1722" data-end="1727">Pop</code> ↔ a <strong data-start="1732" data-end="1752">monoidal functor</strong> mapping spheres into field transformations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1801" data-end="1856">
<p data-start="1803" data-end="1856"><code data-start="1803" data-end="1810">Merge</code> ↔ tensor product in the monoidal structure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1859" data-end="1934">
<p data-start="1861" data-end="1934"><code data-start="1861" data-end="1869">Choice</code> ↔ enrichment in the presheaf topos (probabilistic subobjects).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1936" data-end="2102">
<p data-start="1938" data-end="2102"><strong data-start="1938" data-end="1957">Topos Semantics</strong><br data-start="1957" data-end="1960">
Clarify that typing judgments <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma ⊢ t : A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">Γ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⊢</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span> correspond to morphisms in the presheaf category, with internal logic ensuring soundness.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2104" data-end="2107">
<h2 data-start="2109" data-end="2150">Suggested Formal Layering in the Paper</h2>
<ol data-start="2152" data-end="2509">
<li data-start="2152" data-end="2193">
<p data-start="2155" data-end="2193"><strong data-start="2155" data-end="2169">Section A:</strong> Syntax (BNF grammar).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2194" data-end="2260">
<p data-start="2197" data-end="2260"><strong data-start="2197" data-end="2211">Section B:</strong> Typing system (CoC + probabilistic extension).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2261" data-end="2343">
<p data-start="2264" data-end="2343"><strong data-start="2264" data-end="2278">Section C:</strong> Operational semantics (β-reduction, choice, merge congruence).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2344" data-end="2430">
<p data-start="2347" data-end="2430"><strong data-start="2347" data-end="2361">Section D:</strong> Category-theoretic semantics (your PDF: functorial, 2-cat, topos).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2431" data-end="2509">
<p data-start="2434" data-end="2509"><strong data-start="2434" data-end="2448">Section E:</strong> Soundness and subject reduction (link typing + semantics).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="2511" data-end="2514">
<p data-start="2516" data-end="2849" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="2537" data-end="2573">merge the LaTeX BNF/typing rules</strong> we wrote earlier <em data-start="2591" data-end="2648">directly into the categorical definitions from your PDF</em>, so you end up with one continuous formal system: syntax → typing → semantics → category/topos structure? This would give you a polished “core language + categorical semantics” section for your paper.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px]"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0