<ul data-start="1237" data-end="1481">
<li data-start="1237" data-end="1315">
<p data-start="1239" data-end="1315"><strong data-start="1239" data-end="1255">β-reduction:</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pop}(\mathrm{Sphere}(x{:}A.\,t),u) \to t[u/x]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Sphere</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mord"><span class="mrel">:</span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mord">.</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1316" data-end="1374">
<p data-start="1318" data-end="1374"><strong data-start="1318" data-end="1327">Nest:</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Nest}(t,u) \to \mathrm{Pop}(t,u)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Nest</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Pop</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1375" data-end="1430">
<p data-start="1377" data-end="1430"><strong data-start="1377" data-end="1388">Choice:</strong> reduces to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span> w.p. <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>, else <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1431" data-end="1481">
<p data-start="1433" data-end="1481"><strong data-start="1433" data-end="1443">Merge:</strong> associative, commutative congruence</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1483" data-end="1486">
<h3 data-start="1488" data-end="1539">4. Category-Theoretic Semantics (from your PDF)</h3>
<ul data-start="1540" data-end="2278">
<li data-start="1540" data-end="1718">
<p data-start="1542" data-end="1718"><strong data-start="1542" data-end="1572">Pop as a Monoidal Functor:</strong><br data-start="1572" data-end="1575">
<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi></mrow><mo>:</mo><mtext>Sphere</mtext><mo>→</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>Field</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>Field</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pop} : \text{Sphere} \to [\text{Field}, \text{Field}]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Pop</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Sphere</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Field</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Field</span></span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span><br data-start="1644" data-end="1647">
preserving tensor products and the unit, with coherence isomorphisms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1720" data-end="1994">
<p data-start="1722" data-end="1752"><strong data-start="1722" data-end="1750">Sphere² as a 2-Category:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1755" data-end="1994">
<li data-start="1755" data-end="1809">
<p data-start="1757" data-end="1809">0-cells: regions <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8193em; vertical-align: -0.136em;"></span><span class="mord">Ω</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⊆</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1812" data-end="1855">
<p data-start="1814" data-end="1855">1-cells: spheres (supports + morphisms)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1858" data-end="1924">
<p data-start="1860" data-end="1924">2-cells: natural transformations <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau: \sigma_1 ⇒ \sigma_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1927" data-end="1994">
<p data-start="1929" data-end="1994">Composition: horizontal, vertical, with strict 2-category axioms.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1996" data-end="2278">
<p data-start="1998" data-end="2020"><strong data-start="1998" data-end="2018">Topos Semantics:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2023" data-end="2278">
<li data-start="2023" data-end="2078">
<p data-start="2025" data-end="2078">Category of presheaves <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mtext>op</mtext></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[Sphere^\text{op}, Set]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord mathnormal">Sp</span><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">er</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">op</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2081" data-end="2121">
<p data-start="2083" data-end="2121">Subobject classifier = truth sphere.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2124" data-end="2166">
<p data-start="2126" data-end="2166">Exponentials, finite limits, colimits.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2169" data-end="2278">
<p data-start="2171" data-end="2278">Internal intuitionistic higher-order logic: propositions = subspheres; proofs = morphisms preserving truth.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2280" data-end="2283">
<h3 data-start="2285" data-end="2306">5. Soundness Link</h3>
<ul data-start="2307" data-end="2632">
<li data-start="2307" data-end="2406">
<p data-start="2309" data-end="2406"><strong data-start="2309" data-end="2329">Typing judgments</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma \vdash t : A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">Γ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⊢</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span> correspond to <strong data-start="2368" data-end="2381">morphisms</strong> in the presheaf topos.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2407" data-end="2477">
<p data-start="2409" data-end="2477"><strong data-start="2409" data-end="2424">β-reduction</strong> corresponds to naturality of evaluation morphisms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2478" data-end="2546">
<p data-start="2480" data-end="2546"><strong data-start="2480" data-end="2489">Merge</strong> corresponds to tensor product in the monoidal functor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2547" data-end="2632">
<p data-start="2549" data-end="2632"><strong data-start="2549" data-end="2559">Choice</strong> corresponds to enrichment with probability distributions in the topos.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2634" data-end="2637">
<p data-start="2639" data-end="2688">This structure gives you a <strong data-start="2666" data-end="2687">complete pipeline</strong>:</p>
<p data-start="2690" data-end="2760"><strong data-start="2690" data-end="2760">Syntax → Typing → Operational Semantics → Category/Topos Semantics</strong></p>
<p data-start="2762" data-end="2853">So your PDF’s categorical core is now tightly linked with the BNF/type-theoretic front-end.</p>
