Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Choice}(p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>),D,S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>D,S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and assume
independence via product in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom} : O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is Boolean disjunction,
then for any </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Pr</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom}(R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>,R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>))=D</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
1 - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\prod</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>(1 - p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="4743" data-end="4768"><strong data-start="4743" data-end="4768">How to use this block</strong></p>
<ul data-start="4769" data-end="5124">
<li data-start="4769" data-end="4825">
<p data-start="4771" data-end="4825">Drop it after your “Categorical Semantics” subsection.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4826" data-end="4942">
<p data-start="4828" data-end="4942">It cleanly specifies how <code data-start="4853" data-end="4861">Choice</code> denotes a genuine probability distribution <strong data-start="4905" data-end="4930">in the presheaf topos</strong> (Option B).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4943" data-end="5124">
<p data-start="4945" data-end="5124">It also ties together <code data-start="4967" data-end="4972">Pop</code> (evaluation morphism), <code data-start="4996" data-end="5003">Merge</code> (product), and probabilistic sequencing (<code data-start="5045" data-end="5051">bind</code>), plus a one-line adequacy claim and the independent-channels statement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5126" data-end="5325" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If you want, I can also supply a tiny <strong data-start="5164" data-end="5192">“Meta-theory” subsection</strong> with preservation/progress/adequacy statements formatted as theorems/lemmas so the section reads like a full PL semantics treatment.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C