<p data-start="1784" data-end="1902"><em data-start="1784" data-end="1794">Reading:</em> We push both branches into the monad via <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span></span></span></span>, then combine them by <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">m</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">i</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{mix}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6794em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">mix</span></span></span></span></span> weighted by <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<hr data-start="1904" data-end="1907">
<h3 data-start="1909" data-end="1973">(C) Sequencing (Kleisli bind) — operational vs. denotational</h3>
<p data-start="1974" data-end="2068">This shows that “evaluate then continue” is interpreted by <strong data-start="2033" data-end="2041">bind</strong> in the distribution monad.</p>
