</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Merge}(P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
= pq</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{(1,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>)} + p(1-q)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{(2,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>)}
+ (1-p)q</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{(2,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>)} + (1-p)(1-q)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{(3,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>)},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where each Dirac mass is at the corresponding concatenated vector of the shown
length (underscores emphasize value dependence on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>v,w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\medskip</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Takeaway.}
This instance illustrates Cor.~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{cor:merge-pushforward}: the **type-level
shape** (the length index) evolves by the deterministic map </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>k=n{+}m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> while the
**distribution** over shapes and values is exactly the pushforward of the joint
(independent) distribution under concatenation. The construction is general:
any dependent post-processing </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (e.g.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>zipping, padding, folding) yields a
well-typed SPC term whose semantics is the corresponding pushforward measure.
