In the presheaf topos </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Sphere}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{op},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Set}]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge} is interpreted as the monoidal product:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Merge}(t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
= </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which satisfies the coherence conditions of a symmetric monoidal category. 
Commutativity and associativity hold up to the natural isomorphisms of the 
monoidal structure. In the probabilistic setting, when </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are 
independent distributions, the denotation is the product measure.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="759" data-end="864">This way, it aligns with the earlier <strong data-start="796" data-end="826">Sphere/Pop as Exponentials</strong>, <strong data-start="828" data-end="856">Choice as Convex Mixture</strong>, etc.</p>
