01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Commutative Diagrams (Adequacy Proofs)}

Adequacy of the denotational semantics can be captured by the commutativity of 
a family of diagrams linking operational reduction, type-theoretic derivations, 
and categorical interpretation. The central idea is that for any term </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the 
evaluation of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> operationally and the interpretation of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotationally 
produce the same distribution of outcomes.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Sphere/Pop.}
For abstraction and application, adequacy requires the following diagram to 
commute in the presheaf topos </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{E}=[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Sphere}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{op},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Set}]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> , </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>}"] 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{operational}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,swap,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Pop}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Sphere}(x{:}A.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>t),u)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This diagram formalizes that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-reduction coincides with categorical 
evaluation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Merge.}
For the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge} operator, commutativity is expressed by:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span>"] 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{operational flattening}}"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{monoidal product}}"] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Merge}(t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,equal] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Merge}(t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Operational reduction of parallel branches aligns with the symmetric monoidal 
structure of the topos.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Choice.}
For probabilistic choice, adequacy is guaranteed by bilinearity of convex 
mixtures, captured by:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> p,t,u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>}"] 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{operational sampling}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> [0,1] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,swap,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Choice}(p,t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}(p,a,b)=p</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a+(1-p)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. This diagram ensures 
that stochastic reduction and distribution semantics agree pointwise.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Independent Channels Lemma.}
Finally, adequacy of aggregated risk across independent merges is expressed by:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\prod</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O) 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>"] 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{operational Merge}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n) 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\*</span></span><span>}"] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O) 
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,equal] 
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Safe},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Doom}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom}:O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> 
computes the disjunctive failure. This diagram proves that operational 
probabilities and denotational product measures yield the same aggregated risk.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Summary.}
The commutativity of these diagrams establishes that SPC’s operational semantics 
is adequate with respect to its categorical semantics: abstraction/application 
coincides with exponentials, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge} with monoidal tensor, and 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Choice} with convex mixture in the distribution monad.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
