<h3 data-start="1612" data-end="1630">Why this works</h3>
<ul data-start="1631" data-end="1847">
<li data-start="1631" data-end="1727">
<p data-start="1633" data-end="1727"><code data-start="1633" data-end="1643">tabularx</code> replaces <code data-start="1653" data-end="1656">c</code>/<code data-start="1657" data-end="1660">l</code> with <code data-start="1666" data-end="1669">X</code>, which stretches/wraps text across the available width.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1728" data-end="1794">
<p data-start="1730" data-end="1794">Keeps everything inside <code data-start="1754" data-end="1766">\textwidth</code> without manual shrinking.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1795" data-end="1847">
<p data-start="1797" data-end="1847">Still allows math mode (<code data-start="1821" data-end="1830">$\dots$</code>) inside cells.</p>
</li>
</ul>
