 first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="302">Right — the reason your <code data-start="24" data-end="32">tikzcd</code> diagrams are bleeding into the right margin is that they’re too wide for the page. You can fix this in a few ways without changing the mathematical content. The cleanest is to wrap each <code data-start="219" data-end="227">tikzcd</code> environment in a <code data-start="245" data-end="257">\resizebox</code> or <code data-start="261" data-end="272">adjustbox</code> so it scales to <code data-start="289" data-end="301">\textwidth</code>.</p>
<p data-start="304" data-end="384">Here’s a safe fix using <code data-start="328" data-end="355">\resizebox{\textwidth}{!}</code> from the <code data-start="365" data-end="375">graphicx</code> package:</p>
