<h3 data-start="1992" data-end="2009">What changed:</h3>
<ul data-start="2010" data-end="2368">
<li data-start="2010" data-end="2050">
<p data-start="2012" data-end="2050">Shortened <code data-start="2022" data-end="2037">"operational"</code> → <code data-start="2040" data-end="2049">"oper."</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2051" data-end="2127">
<p data-start="2053" data-end="2127">Replaced <code data-start="2062" data-end="2088">"operational flattening"</code> with <code data-start="2094" data-end="2126">\shortstack{oper.\\flattening}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2128" data-end="2178">
<p data-start="2130" data-end="2178">Used <code data-start="2135" data-end="2153">column sep=small</code> to squeeze horizontally.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2179" data-end="2311">
<p data-start="2181" data-end="2311">Compactified arrows (<code data-start="2202" data-end="2211">(p,t,u)</code> instead of <code data-start="2223" data-end="2246">\langle p,t,u \rangle</code>, <code data-start="2248" data-end="2279">$ \llbracket A \rrbracket^2 $</code> instead of writing two copies).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2312" data-end="2368">
<p data-start="2314" data-end="2368">Kept labels readable but consistent across diagrams.</p>
</li>
</ul>
