x-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="240">The problem is that even with <code data-start="30" data-end="48">column sep=small</code>, TikZCD centers everything and some of your long labels (<code data-start="106" data-end="133">\llbracket ... \rrbracket</code>) push into the margin. You can fix this by <strong data-start="177" data-end="207">constraining diagram width</strong>. The two standard solutions are:</p>
<h3 data-start="242" data-end="310">Option 1: <code data-start="256" data-end="290">\resizebox{\textwidth}{!}{ ... }</code> around each diagram</h3>
